preConditionHook:
// Every one of the last overlapBars bar pairs overlaps the earlier bar by at
// least overlapFraction of THAT bar's range -- Brooks's bar-overlap reading of
// sideways, two-sided trading. The denominator is the older bar's range (one
// subtraction, and an inside bar passes automatically, which is his intent),
// not MinList of the two.
//
// EL, lowercase as the feature register writes it (EasyLanguage is
// case-insensitive): countif(minlist(high, high[1]) - maxlist(low, low[1]) >=
// overlapFraction * (high[1] - low[1]), overlapBars), and the count must equal
// the window. countif counts bars 0..N-1 including the current bar and the counted
// condition is a true SERIES -- at position k the offsets shift, so it tests
// bar k against bar k+1 (EL_FEATURES `countif`, VERIFIED; the frozen-offset
// model was refuted). That series behaviour is what makes one CountIF express
// the whole run, and the loop below reproduces it index for index.
//
// maxlist/minlist are ACCEPTED for selection among tick-grid price operands,
// which is what these are, so the plain comparisons stand in for them. On a
// gap pairOverlap goes negative and the test fails, since the right-hand side
// is never negative -- no clamp needed, and the EasyLanguage twin has none.
//
// At overlapBars = 1 this degenerates to the single-pair rule
// BarOverlapFraction; the run over N pairs is what this rule adds.
overlapCount = 0.0;
for (int k = 0; k < (int)overlapBars; ++k) {
    pairTop = high[k];
    if (high[k + 1] < pairTop) pairTop = high[k + 1];
    pairBottom = low[k];
    if (low[k + 1] > pairBottom) pairBottom = low[k + 1];
    pairOverlap = pairTop - pairBottom;
    if (el_ge(pairOverlap, overlapFraction * (high[k + 1] - low[k + 1]))) {
        overlapCount += 1;
    }
}
